the conflict in South Sudan has taken  almost everything from these people they  had no choice but to take refuge in this  camp it's mostly women and children that  have come here seeking a safety away  from the violence and something to eat  mornings have been very bad since the  fighting broke out we have no food and  we have to survive on wild berries and  roots experts say the food shortages in  South Sudan and now among the most acute  in the world and could lead to the worst  famine in decades and there's no sign  the country's civil war will end soon it  has already hindered farmers from  planting crops that means the situation  is likely to get worse in the coming  months it's intensified bombing and  fighting during the planting season may  june and july is likely to have an  impact on the harvest and family's  ability to feed themselves the UN has  already warned that 50,000 children are  at risk of dying from malnutrition this  year alone the UN says around a billion  dollars is needed to prevent a major  humanitarian crisis
 

